"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K4SN1CT61S0NZ7N\",\"title\":\"Helix — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"BICRS\",\"Helix\",\"Planeteers\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2027\",\"Validated by\",\"Normec Verifavia\",\"->\",\"Project code\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"B42M\",\"approval\":\"12 Dec 2025\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biogenic Carbon Capture and Storage v1.2\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 4 of 4\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"28 Jan 2026\",\"Project Name Change Record\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"11 Dec 2025\",\"Validation Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 Dec 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"30 Oct 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://planeteers.de\",\"t\":\"Planeteers\"},{\"h\":\"https://normecverifavia.com\",\"t\":\"Normec Verifavia\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biogenic-capture-and-storage/1.2\",\"t\":\"Biogenic Carbon Capture and Storage v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JSQEE2D51S0GJ1K\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSQEE2D51S0GJ1K/prj_1K4SN1CT61S0NZ7N/pjd_1KG317YKG1S0CB2V/project_name_change_record.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSQEE2D51S0GJ1K/prj_1K4SN1CT61S0NZ7N/pjd_1KC9K4FXS1S027Y4/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSQEE2D51S0GJ1K/prj_1K4SN1CT61S0NZ7N/pjd_1KC90BDNA1S0ZTYH/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSQEE2D51S0GJ1K/prj_1K4SN1CT61S0NZ7N/pjd_1K8VJ54SB1S0P4S2/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\nHelix\\nPlaneteers\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2027\\nValidated by\\nNormec Verifavia\\n->\\nProject code\\nB42M\\nApproval date\\n12 Dec 2025\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jan 2026 to 31 Dec 2030\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiogenic Carbon Capture and Storage v1.2\\nSummary\\n\\nPlaneteers' first project captures CO₂ from a power plant that burns methane produced through the fermentation of sewage sludge. The captured CO₂ reacts with alkaline material, converting it into dissolved inorganic carbon (DIC) in the form of bicarbonate and carbonate. The resulting solution is released into the ocean, where the carbon remains stored for more than 1,000 years.\\n\\nHetlingen, Germany\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 28 Nov 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2025\\nSite visit\\nCompleted 2025\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2027\\nIN PROGRESS\\nInitial credit issuance\\n\\nIsometric issues credits to the project proponent. The results of the process, including the validation and verification report, will be made available for each project on the Registry.\\n\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n28 Jan 2026\\tProject Name Change Record\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n11 Dec 2025\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Dec 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Oct 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"